sections:
  - label: "Beijing 北京"
    html: |
      <section class="page-hero" style="background-image:url('assets/img/dest-beijing.png');"><div class="container"><span class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="tours.html">Destinations</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Beijing</span><h1>Beijing <span class="zh" style="font-family:var(--font-zh);font-size:0.65em;color:var(--gold);">北京</span></h1><p>China's capital for most of the past eight centuries, Beijing is where imperial grandeur meets modern ambition — golden palaces, a wall across mountains, and hutong lanes that still hum with daily life.</p></div></section>
  - label: "Why visit Beijing?"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/dest-beijing.png" alt="Beijing" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">北<br/>京</div></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Culture & History</span><h2 class="display-h2">Why visit Beijing?</h2><p>China's capital for most of the past eight centuries, Beijing is where imperial grandeur meets modern ambition. The Forbidden City, the Great Wall and the Temple of Heaven are icons the world knows. But the city's real magic hides in its hutong alleyways, its dawn tai chi gatherings, and its dumpling restaurants that have changed nothing in 150 years.</p><p>Nowhere else can you stand on a Ming-dynasty watchtower at sunrise, wander a courtyard tea house by noon, and watch acrobats fly through the air by night — all within the same day.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Beijing at a glance"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;"><div class="container"><div class="stat-strip"><div class="stat-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);"><div class="reveal"><div class="stat-num">8</div><div class="stat-label">Centuries as China's capital — from the Yuan dynasty to the present day</div></div><div class="reveal reveal-d1"><div class="stat-num">7</div><div class="stat-label">UNESCO World Heritage sites within a day's reach of the city</div></div><div class="reveal reveal-d2"><div class="stat-num">21M</div><div class="stat-label">Residents make Beijing one of the world's largest capital cities</div></div><div class="reveal reveal-d3"><div class="stat-num">21,000 km</div><div class="stat-label">Total length of the Great Wall — our favourite section is at Mutianyu</div></div></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Iconic experiences in Beijing"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Must-See Sights</span><h2 class="display-h2">Iconic experiences in Beijing</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>The Forbidden City</h3><p>The world's largest palace complex — 980 buildings, 500 years of emperors, and golden roofs that glow at dusk. Our scholar-guides bring six centuries of drama to life.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>The Great Wall at Mutianyu</h3><p>Skip the crowds at Badaling. We take you to a quieter, fully restored section at dawn — you may have the wall to yourself for an hour.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Temple of Heaven</h3><p>Where Ming emperors prayed for good harvests. Arrive early to see locals practicing tai chi, singing opera, and flying kites.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Summer Palace</h3><p>A lakeside imperial retreat of pavilions, bridges and the famous Long Corridor — best seen by boat with a gentle breeze off Kunming Lake.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Hutong Alleys</h3><p>Ride a rickshaw through courtyard lanes, sip tea in a local's home, and feel the everyday Beijing that guidebooks miss.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>798 Art District</h3><p>Decommissioned factory halls reborn as galleries and design cafés — Beijing's edgy, contemporary counterpoint to its imperial past.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Flavours of the Capital"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-copy reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Food Capital</span><h2 class="display-h2">Flavours of the Capital</h2><p>Beijing's cuisine is hearty and theatrical. The star is Peking duck, roasted over fruit-wood until the skin shatters like glass — our private duck dinner includes the chef's carving show at your table. Beyond duck, the city's dawn markets are a whole world of snacks.</p><p>We take you to the institutions locals actually queue for, not the tourist traps — from a century-old noodle shop to a courtyard dumpling master.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li><strong>Peking duck</strong> — roasted over fruit-wood, carved tableside, wrapped in thin pancakes with scallion</li><li><strong>Zhajiangmian</strong> — wheat noodles tossed with fermented soybean paste and crisp vegetables</li><li><strong>Jiaozi</strong> — boiled or pan-fried dumplings, the beloved northern Chinese staple</li><li><strong>Tanghulu</strong> — candied hawthorn skewers, the classic winter street sweet</li><li><strong>Douzhi</strong> — a fermented mung-bean drink, a true local's breakfast (an acquired taste!)</li></ul></div><div class="split-media reveal reveal-d1"><img src="assets/img/beijing-food.png" alt="Peking duck carved tableside" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">烤<br/>鸭</div></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "A perfect 4-day journey"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--paper-deep);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Sample Itinerary</span><h2 class="display-h2">A perfect 4-day journey</h2><p>Every journey we design is tailor-made — this is a favourite starting point.</p></div><div class="steps-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:22px;"><div class="step reveal"><span class="step-num">01</span><h3>Arrival &amp; First Impressions</h3><p>Private airport transfer, hotel near Qianmen, then an evening stroll along Qianmen Street and Dashilan. Welcome Peking duck dinner to break the journey.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d1"><span class="step-num">02</span><h3>The Imperial Heart</h3><p>The Forbidden City with a history scholar, then climb Jingshan Park for the classic palace panorama. Rickshaw through the hutongs and a dumpling dinner in a courtyard home.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d2"><span class="step-num">03</span><h3>Great Wall &amp; Lakes</h3><p>Dawn drive to Mutianyu Great Wall (cable car up, toboggan down), then the Summer Palace — cruise Kunming Lake and walk the Long Corridor.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d3"><span class="step-num">04</span><h3>Spirit &amp; Departure</h3><p>Temple of Heaven at opening (tai chi and kites), 798 Art District for lunch and modern art, an evening acrobatics show, and a private transfer to the airport.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Beijing after dark"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/beijing-night.png" alt="Beijing hutong lanterns at night" /></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Night Views</span><h2 class="display-h2">Beijing after dark</h2><p>After sunset the capital trades imperial solemnity for neon and night markets. The hutongs glow with red lanterns and hidden cocktail bars; Chaoyang pulses with rooftop lounges; and the city's acrobatics shows are spectacles for every age. We arrange a private evening so you see both the old and the new.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li>Hutong lantern walk with a stop at a hidden courtyard bar</li><li>Chaoyang rooftop lounge overlooking the CBD skyline</li><li>Legendary acrobatics or Kung Fu show with hotel pick-up</li><li>Guijie (Ghost Street) night-market food crawl</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Beyond the city"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Nearby Escapes</span><h2 class="display-h2">Beyond the city</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 18l6-8 4 5 3-4 5 7z"/><path d="M3 21h18"/></svg></div><h3>Gubei Water Town</h3><p>A canal town beneath a restored Great Wall section (Simatai) — magical at night when the walls are lit. 2 h from the city by private car.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Chengde</h3><p>The Qing emperors' vast mountain resort and Eight Outer Temples — a cooler, greener royal retreat. 3 h by high-speed train.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 18h16M6 18V8l6-4 6 4v10"/><path d="M10 18v-4h4v4"/></svg></div><h3>Datong</h3><p>Yungang Grottoes — 50,000 Buddhist carvings — and the vertiginous Hanging Temple clamped to a cliff. 2 h by rail.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Good to know"
    html: |
      <section class="commit-band section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal" style="margin-bottom:20px;"><span class="eyebrow centered">Travel Tips</span><h2 class="display-h2">Good to know before you go</h2></div><div class="commit-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;"><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Getting around</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">The subway is fast and bilingual-signposted, but for the Great Wall and airport we pair you with a private car and English-speaking driver.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Air &amp; seasons</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Spring is short and windy, autumn crisp and blue — our favourite. Winter is cold but crowd-free and superb for the Wall; summers can be hot.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Best viewpoints</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Jingshan Park's hill gives the classic Forbidden City panorama — we time your climb for late-afternoon light.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Local etiquette</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">A courtyard dumpling dinner is the best way to meet Beijinger warmth — shoes off at the threshold, and a cheerful "gan bei!" toast goes a long way.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
